<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_ScaldArmor.xml                      EnvironmentalHazards - FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F1

  greentide_kit_spec.md M3 ("Scald damage + steam devils") calls for a
  dedicated `RM_ScaldArmor` DamageArmorCategoryDef so heat/flame armor
  stats give no protection against a scalding wet burn - "if the greentide
  build slips, the def is XML and ships here first." Checked this pass:
  no `RUT_Scald`/`RM_ScaldArmor` def exists anywhere in the repo yet
  (greentide's own M3 has not landed), so FORGE_MECHANICS_1's own F1 ships
  it, generic and RM_-tier (this mod - mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards -
  is exactly where an RM_-prefixed def belongs per the naming scheme, not
  the RUT_-tier UtinniPatches mod that ships RUT_Scald itself).

  DamageArmorCategoryDef (Verse/DamageArmorCategoryDef.cs, verified this
  pass): armorRatingStat + optional multStat, no DamageWorker override
  needed - vanilla's own ArmorUtility reads DamageDef.armorCategory to
  pick which armor StatDef applies, plain data end to end (settles
  greentide_kit_spec.md's own open ❓ on this point, for whichever kit
  ships the def first).

  multStat left unset - no vendored material in this repo grants scald
  resistance as a Stuff property (unlike vanilla ArmorRating_Heat's own
  StuffPower_Armor_Heat), so there is nothing to multiply by; apparel
  grants this stat via a plain <statBases> entry instead (the wet-kit gear
  the greentide sheet's §7 fireweed-fiber tree owns, not this file).
-->
<Defs>

  <DamageArmorCategoryDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RM_ScaldArmor</defName>
    <armorRatingStat>RM_ArmorRating_Scald</armorRatingStat>
  </DamageArmorCategoryDef>

</Defs>
